{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_overview", "label": "DevTools overview (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "label": "DevTools", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An embeddable web UI attached to a running ActorSystem \u2014 the BEAM observer idea for actor-ts: the process tree, the mailboxes, the load."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtoolsoptions", "label": "DevToolsOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "host, port, auth, ipAllowlist, allowRemote, allowUngatedMount, backend, serveUi, allowedOrigins, panels and uiDevelopmentRoot."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_attach", "label": "DevTools.attach", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Binds a server of its own, which is usually what you want since the DevTools port should be firewalled separately from the application; detach also runs automatically during CoordinatedShutdown, so SIGTERM releases the port."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_mount", "label": "DevTools.mount", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "mount never learns where its routes end up and host is not read on that path, so DevTools cannot tell a private port from a public one and will not guess. It asks for auth, ipAllowlist or allowUngatedMount up front; auth and ipAllowlist wrap the returned tree, so the gate travels with it wherever it is mounted."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "label": "Per-panel switches", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A disabled panel is disabled for good \u2014 its data never leaves the process, whatever a client asks for. Time travel is the one to think about first because it surfaces raw persisted events, followed by dead letters and event stream, which both show message payloads."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "label": "DevTools security posture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loopback by default; a routable bind must be deliberate and the error names all three ways to make it so; gates cover the UI, the JSON endpoints and the WebSocket upgrade alike, since a gate on only the JSON would leave the actual data channel open. The cluster side trusts the connection rather than the message, so a peer that lies can only lie about its own row."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_same_origin_sockets", "label": "Same-origin WebSocket rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A WebSocket handshake is not subject to the same-origin policy, so binding to loopback is no substitute \u2014 any page in the developer browser can reach 127.0.0.1. allowedOrigins widens the rule rather than replacing it, and a request with no Origin is allowed because CSWSH needs a browser and a browser always sends one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_tap_protocol", "label": "Tap protocol over one WebSocket", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All panels speak one versioned wire contract over a single socket, so they share a connection rather than each opening their own."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_no_node_reachable", "label": "No node reachable dialog", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every panel keeps showing its last reading \u2014 the final one before a node died is usually the one worth having \u2014 so a lost connection would otherwise look exactly like a healthy system. The panel dims and the uptime counter freezes rather than counting past the death of the system it measures."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_cost", "label": "What DevTools costs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unused, nothing: creating the extension opens no port and installs no taps, and each panel collects only while a browser is subscribed. While attached it switches the metrics registry on, because throughput, mailbox drops and handler latency read 0 against the default noop registry; detach puts the noop back, and a registry you enabled yourself is left alone in both directions."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_angular_ui", "label": "The Angular + ECharts UI bundle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both are build-time dependencies only and appear in neither dependencies nor peerDependencies, so nothing a consumer installs carries them and the served page loads nothing over the network. ECharts is lazily loaded in its own chunk, and the toolchain is a deliberate separate install so a fresh clone can typecheck, test and smoke without it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_examples_wiring", "label": "DevTools wiring in the examples", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only examples that run until you stop them carry DevTools, so one that finishes on its own can be copied into a project and run unchanged. Seven that only ever attached bound a port and logged a URL dead before a browser could open it; teaching them to park would hand the browser a system already gone, and parking instead of the teardown would delete the demonstration."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtoolsoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_attach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_mount", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtoolsoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_same_origin_sockets", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_tap_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_cost", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_angular_ui", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_no_node_reachable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_devtools", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_examples_wiring", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_mount", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_attach", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_security", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_mtls", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_dead_letters_dead_letters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_event_stream_event_stream", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_configuration_configuration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_overview_panels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observabili